hide circle
hide empty methods

top to bottom direction
title Execution values / cleanup · Processing
class "lifecycle.Claim" as Claim <<frozen execution value>> $PROC {
 job_id: UUID
 attempt_id: UUID
 lease_token: UUID
 owner_id: UUID
 source: dict
 operations: list
 source_url: str
 source_url_expires_at: datetime
 deadline_at: datetime
}
class "processing.models.CleanupIntent" as Cleanup <<cleanup ledger>> $INFRA {
 attempt_id: UUID
 job_id: UUID
 next_try_at: datetime
 tries: int
 created_at: datetime
 retired_at: datetime | None
}
class "processing.lifecycle" as Life <<module>> $PROC {
 claim(factory, job_id, attempt_id, settings)
 live(pair, token, now)
 heartbeat(factory, work, settings)
 finish(factory, work, *, outputs, error)
}
class SubmissionGuard <<independent cancellation root>> $PROC {
 asset_id: UUID
 owner_id: UUID
 job_id: UUID | None
 deleted_at: datetime | None
}
note bottom of SubmissionGuard
 _guard(): create / lock; verify owner.
 Cancel before submit: tombstone without Job.
 Later submit cannot resurrect the asset.
 job_id: nullable local FK, not UNIQUE.
end note
Claim -[hidden]down- Life
Cleanup -[hidden]down- SubmissionGuard
Life ..up> Claim : claim() creates;
Life ..right> Cleanup : cleanup_intent()
note bottom of Claim
  Claim is local worker authority; never a queue payload.
  Frozen fields; nested dict/list remain mutable.
  Lease is Attempt columns, not a Lease class.
  V1 legacy source_url is empty; Source descriptor is used.
end note
note bottom of Cleanup
  Per Attempt: 0..1 intent; per Job: 0..* intents.
  job_id + attempt_id are local FKs.
  finish(error), retry, cancel, interrupt:
  stage intent; recovery scans attempt prefix.
end note
legend bottom
  Dashed = dependency; IDs reference Job / Attempt.
  lock_pair() + live() enforce the heartbeat / finish fences.
endlegend

@enduml
